{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nrebar records NO session identifier on a claim distinct from `assignee` and the event\n`author`. A claim writes a `STATUS(open->in_progress)` (+ `EDIT(assignee)`); the envelope\ncarries `timestamp`, `uuid`, `event_type`, `author` (git user), and `env_id` — but\n`env_id` is the tracker init-environment id (written once at `rebar init`, shared by ALL\nevents), NOT a per-session/per-agent id. So an `in_progress` state cannot be attributed to\nthe specific agent **session** that claimed it.\n\nThe design for this epic is complete (unknowns resolved, experiments run, OSS surveyed).\nFull design doc lives with the driving session; the resolved decisions are below.\n\n## What\nWhen a coding-agent session id is present in the environment, automatically record it on\nthe `open->in_progress` transition so an in_progress ticket is attributable to the session\nthat started it — additively, without disturbing `assignee`/`author`, local-only,\ncompaction-safe, tolerated by older clones.\n\n## Design decisions (resolved)\n- **Env-var contract (ordered, data-driven list).** Explicit rebar var first, then native\n  harness vars by popularity, ambient last: `REBAR_SESSION_ID` -> `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`\n  -> `OPENCODE_SESSION_ID` -> `SESSION_ID` -> None. (`CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE_SESSION_ID` captured\n  as a secondary `remote_session` field.) **Design correction (story 7656):** Codex is NOT a\n  native var in this list — it exposes no supported readable session env var, so it is covered\n  by its SessionStart shim exporting `REBAR_SESSION_ID` instead (there is no `CODEX_THREAD_ID`).\n  Never fall back to git HEAD (changes per commit). One shared resolver replaces today's two\n  divergent ones.\n- **Storage.** Record on the claim `STATUS` event's `data[\"session\"]`; fold to reducer\n  state key `claimed_session` (mirrors `assignee`). No new event type, no envelope change.\n- **Jira.** N/A — a local reducer-state key never enters the reconciler (outbound differ\n  is an explicit allow-list).\n- **Reliable capture.** `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` is an env var only in the remote runner;\n  the local CLI needs a SessionStart hook that exports `REBAR_SESSION_ID`.\n\n## Context (gotchas to respect — from OSS prior art)\n- Session ids are NOT stable across `--resume`/`--continue`/fork/subagents; treat the\n  record as \"the session that emitted this claim event\", not a per-ticket lifetime id.\n- A leaked/stale env var pollutes unrelated sessions (rebar bug 76e9 class) — prefer\n  hook-injected, session-scoped values.\n- Keep it local-only + opaque (consent/provenance sensitivity); read the var as a plain\n  string, never interpolate/execute it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Decomposed into discrete-deliverable child stories parented to THIS epic (via each\n      child's `parent_id`, confirmable with `rebar deps 38ec-5f12-fdf5-4340`): S1\n      `6014-0863-2e36-41b3`, S2 `68ef-da4f-b64b-4903`, S3 `199b-f56f-5ba1-468b`, S5\n      `c557-8f46-0c16-4bf5`, S4 `ec5c-bd06-aa49-42d0`, S6 `7656-0a67-e881-4131`, plus the\n      module-size split refactor `458f-5b67-961e-4e80` — all closed.\n- [x] Env-var contract implemented as the ordered, extensible resolver above\n      (`REBAR_SESSION_ID -> CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID -> OPENCODE_SESSION_ID -> SESSION_ID`, with\n      Codex covered by its `REBAR_SESSION_ID` shim rather than a native `CODEX_THREAD_ID` — see\n      `src/rebar/_commands/session_id.py`).\n- [x] Storage shape implemented (STATUS `data[\"session\"]` -> `claimed_session` state).\n- [x] Claim/transition records the id when present; no-op when absent.\n- [x] Read surface exposes the claiming session id for a ticket.\n- [x] Backward/forward compatible + compaction-safe (regression-tested).\n- [x] Local-CLI capture shim ships (Claude Code), plus Codex/Cursor shims.\n- [ ] A claim made while a recognized session env var is set durably records that session\n- [ ] Absent the env var, behavior is byte-for-byte unchanged (fully backward compatible).\n- [ ] The recorded id survives compaction and is preserved-and-ignored by older clones.\n- [ ] Works in the LOCAL Claude Code CLI (not only the remote runner), via a capture shim.\n- [ ] Session id is attributable across the popular OSS harnesses (Claude Code, OpenCode,"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007093431194001,"uuid":"5ce89f4c-95e3-4518-8895-c7b39b578a94"}